course: dictionary
lesson: 15174
title: Words for cleaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scrubbing means cleaning something by rubbing it hard, usually with a brush and soap or water. «Mum is scrubbing the pots at the sink.» The clue is that she is rubbing hard, not just wiping them.
explain: Scrubbing can also be a noun, meaning one act of cleaning in this way. «The bath needs a good scrubbing.» The word good tells you it should be a thorough, hard clean, not a quick wipe.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «Keep scrubbing until the mud comes off your boots.» If you put in "rubbing hard" and the sentence still makes sense, you have got it right.
fact: Scrubbing means cleaning by rubbing hard.
fact: A scrubbing is one act of cleaning in this way: «The floor needed a scrubbing.»
fact: Scrubbing is the -ing form of the verb scrub: scrub, scrubs, scrubbed, scrubbing.
fact: A scrubbing brush is a brush used for scrubbing dirt off things.
fact: Scrubbing your hands for at least 20 seconds helps to remove germs.
exercise: «Dad is scrubbing the bath with soap.» What is Dad doing? | Painting it bright blue | Looking at his face in it | *Cleaning it by rubbing hard | Filling it with water to swim
exercise: Mum says, «The pots need a good scrubbing.» What does a good scrubbing mean? | *A hard, thorough clean | A loud noise | A quick look at the pots | A long nap
exercise: «Ava is scrubbing the muddy boots with a brush.» Find and copy the word that means cleaning by rubbing hard. | muddy | *scrubbing | boots | brush
test: «Wash your hands well, and keep scrubbing for at least 20 seconds.» Why should you keep scrubbing? | To get a sticker | To make the soap smell nice | *To remove germs | To make your hands dry
test: Which word is the -ing form of scrub? | scrubbed | scrub | scrubs | *scrubbing
exam: «Grandma spent the whole morning scrubbing the kitchen floor until it shone.» What does scrubbing mean here? | Painting the floor a new colour | *Cleaning by rubbing hard | Walking carefully across the floor | Quickly sweeping up dust
